I am currently building my foundation in cybersecurity by studying both theoretical concepts and practical security techniques. My learning so far has covered networking, cryptography, Linux and PowerShell fundamentals, malware, ransomware protection, system security, wireless security, and social engineering.

🌐 Networking

I studied the fundamentals of computer networking and how devices communicate with each other.

Topics covered include:

Basic networking concepts
IP addresses and MAC addresses
TCP/IP fundamentals
Common network protocols
Ports and services
Client-server communication
Basic network troubleshooting
Understanding how network traffic flows between systems

Understanding networking is an important foundation for cybersecurity because many security attacks and defensive techniques depend on how systems communicate over a network.

🔐 Cryptography

I learned the fundamentals of cryptography and how it is used to protect information.

Topics covered include:

Encryption and decryption
Symmetric encryption
Asymmetric encryption
Keys and their importance
Digital signatures
Confidentiality, Integrity, and Authentication
Basic understanding of cryptographic algorithms

I also learned how cryptography is used in real-world security applications to protect sensitive data and communications.

#️⃣ Hashing

I studied hashing and its importance in cybersecurity and digital forensics.

Topics covered include:

What hashing is
Hash functions
MD5
SHA-1
SHA-256
File integrity verification
Password hashing
Difference between hashing and encryption

I learned that hashes can be used to verify whether a file has been modified and are particularly useful in areas such as digital forensics and malware analysis.

