🛡️ Ransomware Protection

I studied how ransomware attacks work at a basic level and how devices can be protected against them.

Defensive strategies I learned include:

Keeping operating systems and applications updated
Using reliable security software
Maintaining regular backups
Using strong authentication
Avoiding suspicious attachments and links
Applying the principle of least privilege
Monitoring unusual system activity
Isolating infected systems
Maintaining offline or protected backups

This helped me understand that cybersecurity is not only about detecting attacks but also about preventing attacks and reducing their impact.

